  "question": {
    "text": "One conducting U tube can slide inside another as shown in figure, maintaining electrical contacts between the tubes. The magnetic field $B$ is perpendicular to the plane of the figure. if each tube moves towards the other at a constant speed V, then the emf induced in the circuit in terms of $B, \\ell$ and $\\mathrm{V}$ where $\\ell$ is the width of each tube will be\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0134_1689a52fc7f6.png\"><br>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{B}\\ell \\mathrm{V}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-\\mathrm{B}\\ell \\mathrm{V}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nzero\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$2 \\mathrm{B}\\ell \\mathrm{V}$",
      "is_correct": true
